Ladybird gives a range input a natural size of 129px by 16px in its
writing mode, which zoom scales, and no UA width or height. The 129px
is the track length Blink and WebKit use, so the default size matches
theirs exactly: Blink’s LayoutBox::DefaultIntrinsicContentInlineSize()
answers SliderIntrinsicInlineSize(), 129px times the zoom, for any
range input, and WebKit’s RenderSlider::computeIntrinsicLogicalWidths()
takes defaultTrackLength, also 129. Gecko’s nsRangeFrame sizes it at
12em by 1.3em, and its IntrinsicISize() resolves a percentage inline
size against zero for the min-content size, as Ladybird now does for
a slider. Run in Chrome 157.0.8103.79, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5:
Ladybird matches Chrome in every case in the test; Firefox stretches the
same cases at its own size.
